You should use the single dagger to fight in melee in the beginning.  Also,
keep the rest of the daggers in the quiver to fire.  You want to split the
dagger pile so that if you get hit by rust trap or rust monster, only 1
dagger is affected and not the entire pile of dagger you have.  You want to
bring the dagger skill up to expert first, then work on two-weapon.  Also
remember this means you should be using a shield as well.

Daggers are extremely good early weapon, since it comes with +2 to hit bonus
naturally, and in the early game you do miss fairly frequently.  You
shouldn't need any other weapon.

Also, remember when monster is fleeing, you want to un-#twoweapon yourself,
so that you get the backstabbing bonus.  You get the bonus even when you are
throwing daggers, but you must be fighting one handed.

